Constructing that keeps it busy so Garmin Wing can attack the Trojan Horde.

01:13:49.680 --> 01:13:50.080
Let's go!

01:13:50.220 --> 01:13:51.020
Garmin Wing, move in!

01:13:58.050 --> 01:13:59.770
Sounds like he said they've launched the white one.

01:14:00.120 --> 01:14:01.500
Let's go. We're joining the action.

01:14:01.850 --> 01:14:03.730
We're launching the Komu Sai immediately, Doran.

01:14:03.850 --> 01:14:05.330
Captain Garma's going to need my help.

01:14:05.570 --> 01:14:05.970
Yes, sir.

01:14:12.100 --> 01:14:14.460
I guess by now these guys are beginning to get the idea

01:14:14.460 --> 01:14:17.040
that Gundam isn't just an ordinary mobile suit.

01:14:17.460 --> 01:14:21.310
Huh? I must be seeing things.

01:14:21.470 --> 01:14:23.090
There's no way a mobile suit can fly.

01:14:27.890 --> 01:14:29.960
Unbelievable. A mobile suit that...

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:35.960
can fight in the air. What? You heard right. Gundam is flying. Amuro has engaged in aerial

01:14:35.960 --> 01:14:40.800
combat. Notify gun tank and gun cannon to cover for Gundam when he comes back down to rebound.

01:14:41.000 --> 01:14:47.250
Do you copy, Ryu? Copy loud and clear. Amuro needs some cover. Fire! Gotcha, Ryu. We have

01:14:47.250 --> 01:14:55.200
to keep all those dops away until he's airborne. All we gotta do is keep the dops away. Nothing

01:14:55.200 --> 01:14:58.800
difficult about that. Hurry up. Hurry.

01:15:03.070 --> 01:15:05.890
Shao wasn't kidding. Those Fettis have themselves one hell of a weapon there.

01:15:12.760 --> 01:15:13.160
Whoa!

01:15:23.470 --> 01:15:26.550
Limgo, the Gundam almost seems to be invincible, doesn't it, Bright?

01:15:26.830 --> 01:15:29.970
Yes. I've never seen anything like it, and I'm sure the enemy hasn't either.

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:32.040
I bet they wish they hadn't started this war.

01:15:32.180 --> 01:15:35.760
Go, Amaral. Defeat the enemy.

01:15:43.820 --> 01:15:45.040
Sha's supposed to be here.

01:15:45.450 --> 01:15:47.570
You want more?

01:15:47.960 --> 01:15:57.680
Try something else.

01:16:00.090 --> 01:16:01.270
I refuse to believe it.

01:16:01.540 --> 01:16:03.240
That monster wiped us out completely.

01:16:03.520 --> 01:16:06.820
He mustn't get through the white base.

01:16:08.510 --> 01:16:08.830
Now!

01:16:16.540 --> 01:16:18.400
Once we get them separated and isolated,

01:16:18.500 --> 01:16:19.860
we can pick them off one by one.

01:16:20.140 --> 01:16:23.270
Sir, the Komasai is closing on Gundam.

01:16:23.450 --> 01:16:25.250
They have the Red Comet Zaku on board,

01:16:25.350 --> 01:16:27.050
and Gundam has lost his beam rifle, sir.

01:16:27.270 --> 01:16:28.530
All right, now what?

01:16:29.200 --> 01:16:29.960
Launch a new right...

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:37.210
up at once the red comet is coming Amuro we're sending you a new beam rifle be

01:16:37.210 --> 01:16:43.070
prepared for it we'll give you whatever supporting cover we can okay gotcha it

01:16:43.070 --> 01:16:52.010
looks like Shaw is planning to drop in on you from 12 o'clock high we're all

01:16:52.010 --> 01:16:54.170
ready to launch the laser rifle sir launch away

01:17:03.160 --> 01:17:06.580
Where's the rifle? Here it comes. I hear it homing in.

01:17:30.030 --> 01:17:31.770
Hmm, the charge keeps bottoming out.

01:17:31.990 --> 01:17:32.370
Ow!

01:17:35.330 --> 01:17:38.270
Launching a missile door has to cover you so you can return to White Base.

01:17:38.650 --> 01:17:40.130
Pull back, Amoro, pull back.

01:17:40.270 --> 01:17:41.350
I won't run away.

01:17:41.590 --> 01:17:43.750
The Xeons have called back all surviving units.

01:17:43.930 --> 01:17:45.010
The battle's over, Amoro.

01:17:45.400 --> 01:17:46.820
You got lucky again, Sha.

01:18:03.260 --> 01:18:06.310
Damn, have to recharge.

01:18:06.590 --> 01:18:07.370
Garma calling Shaw.

01:18:08.070 --> 01:18:08.970
Yes, go ahead.

01:18:09.440 --> 01:18:11.260
Disengage and return to the Gao immediately.

01:18:11.970 --> 01:18:13.310
We have to rethink our plan of attack.

01:18:13.850 --> 01:18:15.490
Their new mobile suit is just incredible.

01:18:16.100 --> 01:18:17.040
That's the word for it.

01:18:17.180 --> 01:18:19.090
I need you. Will you help me out?

01:18:22.220 --> 01:18:23.760
Yes, of course I will.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:30.340
What the?

01:18:33.440 --> 01:18:35.020
...mobblesuit. Do you read me?

01:18:36.020 --> 01:18:38.020
Discontinue pursuit and return to White Base.

01:18:38.360 --> 01:18:39.400
Consider that an order.

01:18:41.340 --> 01:18:42.280
Hey, who's she?

01:18:42.960 --> 01:18:45.100
And how in the world does she know about White Base?

01:18:45.360 --> 01:18:53.100
I'll be taking all the wounded refugees

01:18:53.100 --> 01:18:56.080
as well as several members of Lieutenant Reed's crew from the Solomus.

01:18:56.260 --> 01:18:57.780
Thirty-five individuals in all.

01:18:59.220 --> 01:18:59.980
White Base...

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.800
...with its three mobile suits is to remain here for the time being.

01:19:03.320 --> 01:19:07.820
Now, Admiral Reviel wants complete copies of your battle reports delivered to him immediately.

01:19:08.360 --> 01:19:11.060
Begging your pardon, Lieutenant Matilda? I don't get it.

01:19:11.690 --> 01:19:14.990
Why is White Base being left in this situation with an amateur crew?

01:19:15.540 --> 01:19:18.880
Well, for one thing, Admiral Reviel has been observing this crew...

01:19:18.880 --> 01:19:22.820
...and he's been very impressed with the capable manner in which they've been operating White Base.

01:19:23.050 --> 01:19:25.810
He's confident that they're as reliable as regular troops.

01:19:26.230 --> 01:19:29.980
You have your orders. From Admiral Reviel, Jabro is no longer...

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:34.280
involved in the management of the war. This war has the Federation in a state of confusion.

01:19:34.560 --> 01:19:39.550
That's just another way of saying we're losing the war, Lieutenant. So, if you manage to escape to

01:19:39.550 --> 01:19:45.380
the West, we'll try to resupply you. There's no guarantee. Remember one thing. You will always

01:19:45.380 --> 01:19:49.420
have someone in the forces who is genuinely interested in your welfare and is looking out

01:19:49.420 --> 01:19:56.540
for you. I feel I know you. Do you really? Who knows? Perhaps you're an Esper with hidden memories

01:19:56.540 --> 01:19:59.300
of other lives and other dimensions. You're very brave.

01:20:00.060 --> 01:20:02.140
Had you not fought so well, we could have been killed.

01:20:03.140 --> 01:20:03.880
It was nothing.

01:20:03.960 --> 01:20:05.120
I'm proud of you, Romero.

01:20:05.400 --> 01:20:06.650
Um, what?

01:20:58.440 --> 01:20:58.740
Ciao.

01:21:00.030 --> 01:21:04.600
Yeah, I really don't know how to thank you enough when I owe my very existence to your help.

01:21:04.910 --> 01:21:06.510
Why aren't we being melodramatic?

01:21:06.900 --> 01:21:07.820
You fought bravely.

01:21:08.060 --> 01:21:10.120
We were both lucky to get out of there in one piece.

01:21:10.630 --> 01:21:12.110
Don't worry, we'll get back at him.

01:21:12.540 --> 01:21:14.420
Sounds like you've been hatching a plan.

01:21:14.760 --> 01:21:17.220
If that's the case, I hope you're counting me in on it.

01:21:17.870 --> 01:21:19.250
That's what I'd hope you'd say.

01:21:19.780 --> 01:21:22.320
You know, I'd rather have you back me up than any hundred others.

01:21:22.750 --> 01:21:25.970
With your assistance, I know that I can prove my worth to my sister, Kishiria.

01:21:26.350 --> 01:21:26.710
Kishiria.

01:21:26.950 --> 01:21:29.570
Why is her opinion your only gauge of your own self-esteem?

01:21:30.090 --> 01:21:30.710
Never mind.

01:21:30.960 --> 01:21:31.380
Sorry.

01:21:32.380 --> 01:21:34.000
I'll see you later at the dinner party tonight.

01:21:39.020 --> 01:21:42.060
Parties seem to play a vital role in your occupation policy.

01:21:45.630 --> 01:21:59.980
If your father, Duke Dagan, should ever visit Earth, we'd be...

01:22:00.030 --> 01:22:01.690
It's an honor to offer him our services, too.

01:22:01.990 --> 01:22:03.410
Thank you, I'll be sure to tell him.

01:22:03.570 --> 01:22:06.730
With the usual discounts and side benefits, naturally.

01:22:13.460 --> 01:22:15.620
Pardon me, I'll tell my father.

01:22:17.010 --> 01:22:17.210
Oh!

01:22:18.670 --> 01:22:21.270
That must be the most handsome man in the whole universe.

01:22:21.310 --> 01:22:21.730
Oh, my!

01:22:21.970 --> 01:22:23.440
I think I'm gonna faint.

01:22:26.240 --> 01:22:28.180
It's lucky for you they don't know they've been invaded.

01:22:28.720 --> 01:22:29.860
You'd have a riot to put down.

01:22:30.280 --> 01:22:32.660
I know, but we're covering such an immense area,

01:22:32.700 --> 01:22:34.600
we simply don't have the manpower to track him down.

01:22:35.140 --> 01:22:36.960
Well, now, who's the pompous bigwig?

01:22:37.440 --> 01:22:39.400
Not really. There's a better way to do it.

01:22:40.540 --> 01:22:42.220
That's Eschenbach. He used to be the mayor.

01:22:42.830 --> 01:22:44.650
He despises us zeons with a passion,

01:22:44.860 --> 01:22:47.020
but he's staying on to support his people's interests.

01:22:47.160 --> 01:22:52.640
Ladies and gentlemen, it's my honor to present Miss Iserita Eschenbach.

01:22:52.860 --> 01:22:54.640
Oh, so cute.

01:22:55.340 --> 01:22:57.080
I've never seen Miss Iserita.

01:22:57.120 --> 01:22:57.960
Miss Iserita.

01:22:59.020 --> 01:22:59.280
Oh.

01:23:00.380 --> 01:23:02.620
Please excuse me for just a moment, shall I?

01:23:24.840 --> 01:23:27.440
So he'll never let his daughter marry the son of a Xi'an leader?

01:23:27.870 --> 01:23:28.530
That's right.

01:23:29.100 --> 01:23:29.960
I expected that from...

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:34.520
your father but how do you feel karma i don't care anything about politics the only thing i know is

01:23:34.520 --> 01:23:41.660
i love you nothing else in life matters to me i want to be with you forever i love you darling if

01:23:42.540 --> 01:23:47.590
my father forces me to choose between him and you my choice will be you dear i feel the same way

01:23:47.590 --> 01:23:53.190
but i can't defy my father's army i have to capture the federation's secret weapon and then turn the

01:23:53.190 --> 01:23:59.510
plans over to my father after that father will give me anything you'll see i'm sure he will

01:24:00.380 --> 01:24:01.380
But if he won't...

01:24:01.950 --> 01:24:03.890
I will renounce my allegiance to my father.

01:24:04.680 --> 01:24:07.280
And I'll leave this eon and live here with you.

01:24:07.630 --> 01:24:10.140
Oh, dear Garma, kiss me.

01:24:18.390 --> 01:24:18.770
Garma!

01:24:18.850 --> 01:24:20.100
Huh? What do you want?

01:24:20.430 --> 01:24:21.510
Sorry, sir, did I...

01:24:21.510 --> 01:24:22.490
Deliver your message, soldier.

01:24:23.140 --> 01:24:25.800
It's the Trojan horse, sir. It was spotted in Sector 3.

01:24:26.000 --> 01:24:26.200
What?

01:24:26.870 --> 01:24:29.970
If they get through our border defense and make it into the airspace defended by the...

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:31.940
Fettis. We won't be able to recapture the...

01:24:31.940 --> 01:24:33.420
Enough. Tell Commander Shaw

01:24:33.420 --> 01:24:35.500
and alert my personal mobile air wing.

01:24:35.980 --> 01:24:38.340
The enemy is behaving precisely as I had anticipated

01:24:38.340 --> 01:24:40.440
they would. I'll always be one step

01:24:40.440 --> 01:24:41.980
ahead. Start moving out. Sir!

01:24:43.310 --> 01:24:45.700
Oh, Karma. This is just the opportunity

01:24:45.700 --> 01:24:47.960
that I've been waiting for. I'll capture the Fettis

01:24:47.960 --> 01:24:49.940
secret weapons and I'll return to Zeon again with my

01:24:49.940 --> 01:24:51.850
beautiful bride-to-be. Darling.

01:24:53.640 --> 01:24:54.080
Karma.

01:25:12.570 --> 01:25:12.890
I don't know.

01:25:33.840 --> 01:25:37.640
Well, I guess we should feel extremely flattered that they sent a whole battalion to stop us from getting away.

01:25:37.840 --> 01:25:40.040
I guess it's an honor I could do without, though.

01:25:41.190 --> 01:25:42.250
Send out the Gundam.

01:25:42.740 --> 01:25:45.640
They'd all come after me, and I could keep them busy while you get away.

01:25:46.100 --> 01:25:48.860
No, that would be suicide, and I won't allow it.

01:25:48.940 --> 01:25:49.160
Right.

01:25:49.770 --> 01:25:50.030
Huh?

01:25:50.270 --> 01:25:52.210
An alert from the long-range matter detector.

01:25:52.460 --> 01:25:54.660
There are more planes moving in from the north.

01:25:54.870 --> 01:25:56.590
We can't just sit here defenseless, Noah.

01:25:56.810 --> 01:25:58.230
You have to send Gundam out.

01:25:58.520 --> 01:25:59.980
I can lead them inland while you take...

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:00.980
Take White Base out to sea.

01:26:01.420 --> 01:26:03.460
A decoy operation is just too obvious.

01:26:03.680 --> 01:26:05.360
They'd never be taken in by some...

01:26:11.170 --> 01:26:12.860
Flares? Are they meant for us?

01:26:19.810 --> 01:26:24.320
Hey, look. There's a sports dome up ahead.

01:26:24.460 --> 01:26:26.560
And it's just big enough to conceal White Base.

01:26:26.660 --> 01:26:28.120
I have it on the night scope. You're right.

01:26:28.260 --> 01:26:29.960
Mirai, it'll be tricky, but I think it...

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:31.810
It can be done. Are you willing to try?

01:26:31.970 --> 01:26:33.030
I'll do my darndest.

01:26:33.620 --> 01:26:37.280
Call battle positions. If at all possible, we'll avoid confrontation.

01:26:37.640 --> 01:26:42.080
Mobile suits stand by. Our greatest concern is the safety of the civilians we have on board.

01:26:42.180 --> 01:26:43.920
I think you're forgetting that I'm a civilian.

01:26:44.270 --> 01:26:46.650
Order the crew to level one red alert at once.

01:26:46.810 --> 01:26:50.010
We'll go on silent running. I don't want to hear a sound out of anyone.

01:26:57.960 --> 01:26:59.980
Gun tag and gun cannon on the police down.

01:27:00.060 --> 01:27:02.140
Give me a 180. We'll back her in.

01:27:02.480 --> 01:27:04.240
Computer, stand by for parking maneuver.

01:27:37.900 --> 01:27:38.980
Where's her mother, Retsu?

01:27:39.730 --> 01:27:41.630
There, there, now. Don't cry.

01:27:41.950 --> 01:27:44.690
We'll find your mommy. Everything's going to be just fine.

01:27:44.710 --> 01:27:46.070
Kika! Where's my baby?

01:27:46.170 --> 01:27:46.730
She's all right.

01:27:46.910 --> 01:27:48.620
Oh, thank you. Thank you.

01:27:49.240 --> 01:27:50.960
There, now. She'll be okay.

01:27:57.950 --> 01:27:59.980
Couldn't just disappear. It's the size of a...

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:05.270
small mountain split up and surround the city. They mustn't get away. I believe a little carpet

01:28:05.270 --> 01:28:10.500
bombing might be effective in driving them out into the open, Captain. All units, initiate

01:28:10.500 --> 01:28:13.780
roller shift maneuvers and prepare to bomb every square inch of the entire area.

01:28:40.460 --> 01:28:42.580
Okay everyone, try to stay completely quiet.

01:28:42.860 --> 01:28:48.560
This isn't working, we'll just sit here and be destroyed without fighting back.

01:29:10.520 --> 01:29:12.880
Don't try to stop me. Quit treating me like I'm still a child.

01:29:13.040 --> 01:29:16.620
Please understand, Miss Eschenbach. We're only following orders.

01:29:16.940 --> 01:29:18.220
The mayor sent us to bring you back.

01:29:24.410 --> 01:29:25.910
Don't resist us, Miss Eschenbach.

01:29:26.170 --> 01:29:28.850
Your father is waiting for you. He's worried about you.

01:29:28.990 --> 01:29:29.970
You cannot marry the...

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:31.620
You're the son of our people's number one enemy.

01:29:35.710 --> 01:29:38.490
Child father, my life is my own to govern.

01:29:39.520 --> 01:29:42.800
Let me go. Kidnapping's illegal even if you are my father.

01:29:43.020 --> 01:29:45.460
You'll govern your life exactly as I tell you.

01:29:45.680 --> 01:29:49.140
I am your father. You will show me respect, little lady.

01:29:49.600 --> 01:29:52.900
I want her locked in her room and kept under constant guard till further notice.

01:30:04.510 --> 01:30:06.720
So, what have you got? Is there any sign of white base?

01:30:06.880 --> 01:30:08.660
Nothing. No sound, no movement.

01:30:09.040 --> 01:30:13.060
Damn! Where did they go, Shaw? They've disappeared.

01:30:13.630 --> 01:30:16.960
They're smart, and they're beginning to learn the basics of military strategy.

01:30:17.510 --> 01:30:19.810
I'm going to have to go down there and draw them out myself.

01:30:20.150 --> 01:30:24.010
No. Remember your officer's training. As your subordinate, it's my job to go down there.

01:30:24.200 --> 01:30:25.300
Are you volunteering, Shaw?

01:30:25.460 --> 01:30:27.940
No, it's my job. I don't have to volunteer for it.

01:30:28.020 --> 01:30:29.980
I'm not your commander. Your responsibility...

01:30:30.000 --> 01:30:32.020
is to my brother Dozel, or have you forgotten?

01:30:32.400 --> 01:30:33.260
It should be me.

01:30:33.780 --> 01:30:36.000
Your ambition has made you more hasty than wise.

01:30:36.510 --> 01:30:38.830
Don't let your desire for a woman interfere with your career.

01:30:39.440 --> 01:30:40.140
Try to relax.

01:30:42.010 --> 01:30:42.690
You win.

01:30:42.930 --> 01:30:43.970
I'll find Trojan Horse.

01:30:47.110 --> 01:30:49.470
This has nothing to do with Isarina. Ridiculous.

01:30:50.320 --> 01:30:51.740
I control my own destiny.

01:30:51.900 --> 01:30:54.180
Zaku Ambak system standing by for drop.

01:30:55.250 --> 01:30:58.100
Shaw, the moment you spot the Trojan Horse

01:30:58.100 --> 01:30:59.960
or even one of the mobile suits, let me know.

01:31:00.190 --> 01:31:01.130
and I will bring them down.

01:31:01.370 --> 01:31:03.030
As always, I'm at your command, sir.

01:31:03.290 --> 01:31:04.130
I'll do as you order.

01:31:04.770 --> 01:31:06.090
Thanks for seeing me off, Captain.

01:31:06.380 --> 01:31:07.760
I appreciate it very much.

01:31:09.020 --> 01:31:10.310
Good luck to you, friend.

01:31:11.420 --> 01:31:13.800
May the glory of victory be yours, Captain Garma.

01:31:28.900 --> 01:31:29.980
Three Zakus have been dropped.

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:31.400
and are headed right this way, Bright.

01:31:31.580 --> 01:31:33.180
One of them appears to be Sean's.

01:31:33.240 --> 01:31:35.200
Attention! Three Zakus are approaching.

01:31:35.560 --> 01:31:36.320
Prepare to launch.

01:31:36.460 --> 01:31:38.220
Lure them forward of white base if you can.

01:31:38.640 --> 01:31:39.440
Roger, Wilco.

01:31:39.890 --> 01:31:59.810
What a pity.

01:32:00.250 --> 01:32:03.710
I feel guilty about tricking my own men so shamefully, but I couldn't help it.

01:32:04.050 --> 01:32:07.350
So then, I'm sure the Fettis must have launched their mobile suits by now.

01:32:07.910 --> 01:32:17.930
You're bound to have heard me.

01:32:20.670 --> 01:32:22.410
Look at it. What a wasteland.

01:32:22.910 --> 01:32:23.790
Shah must be here.

01:32:39.600 --> 01:32:41.300
These are real professional military people.

01:32:48.030 --> 01:32:49.090
Improved a bit, hasn't he?

01:32:49.540 --> 01:32:50.660
We'd better take him out quick.

01:33:14.780 --> 01:33:19.910
bad i'm impressed whoever that pilot is he's learning very quickly better check over there

01:33:19.910 --> 01:33:29.960
he's obviously trying to lead us away from it nice strategy it could

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:35.490
worked I spotted the Trojan horse in no

01:33:35.490 --> 01:33:36.970
man's land headed toward the border

01:33:36.970 --> 01:33:39.110
intercepted you're on our way right now

01:33:39.110 --> 01:33:47.640
let's charge your beam cannons and move

01:33:47.640 --> 01:33:59.970
into attack formation the enemy is in a

01:34:00.000 --> 01:34:03.220
formation but they're moving away from us it's our chance to surprise them from

01:34:03.220 --> 01:34:09.460
behind activate all units gun tank gun cannon and all white base batteries

01:34:09.460 --> 01:34:12.440
charge your weapons and target for mass barrage on my mark

01:34:52.110 --> 01:34:54.710
We're taking heavy beam fire from behind us, Captain.

01:34:54.830 --> 01:34:55.750
From behind? You sure?

01:34:56.070 --> 01:34:57.530
It's the Trojan horse, sir.

01:34:57.790 --> 01:34:59.310
Somehow they snuck behind us.

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:01.240
Bring us higher! Get us out of their range!

01:35:01.260 --> 01:35:02.100
Not enough power!

01:35:03.950 --> 01:35:05.550
Bring us about 180 degrees!

01:35:06.750 --> 01:35:10.090
We can still win if we take the Gow into a head-on collision with the Trojan horse!

01:35:29.020 --> 01:35:29.860
Garma, nothing.

01:35:30.030 --> 01:35:35.620
Impersonal you can blame this on the family name you were born with sure you betrayed me. That's right old friend

01:35:35.620 --> 01:35:37.700
But why it doesn't make any sense

01:35:37.700 --> 01:35:42.520
It doesn't have to make any sense to you garma your father will understand and that's all that really matters

01:35:47.970 --> 01:35:50.050
Father you dishonor my family

01:36:00.000 --> 01:36:08.540
that I am worthy of the Zabby family name at last enemy ship approaching on

01:36:08.540 --> 01:36:13.690
head-on collision course he's what that's unbelievable a kamikaze run take us

01:36:13.690 --> 01:36:28.340
higher execute bell evasion maneuver let's take cover

01:36:32.140 --> 01:36:34.400
With this deed, I show all I have truly won.

01:37:01.920 --> 01:37:04.940
Thank heaven. We're alive. We made it.

01:37:06.750 --> 01:37:16.950
And you're sure he was? Of course. Thank you.

01:37:18.440 --> 01:37:19.020
Yes, Sarina.

01:37:20.980 --> 01:37:21.560
Yes, father.

01:37:23.010 --> 01:37:25.120
Garma. Garma has been killed in action.

01:38:07.870 --> 01:38:12.070
Garma, youngest son of Duke Dagon Soto-Zabi, was dead.

01:38:13.060 --> 01:38:16.680
The Duchy of Zion observed deep mourning for the fallen land.

01:38:17.620 --> 01:38:20.860
It was said that Duke Dagon received the news without a word.

01:38:21.560 --> 01:38:26.740
His grief was revealed only by the fact that he let his cane slip from his grasp.

01:38:27.660 --> 01:38:29.980
The Duke ordered his eldest son, Giran,

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:32.000
to call the Zabi family together.

01:38:46.630 --> 01:38:48.730
Everything's just as it was six months ago.

01:38:49.090 --> 01:38:50.650
No progress or improvement whatsoever.

01:39:09.630 --> 01:39:13.050
My brother Garma must not have sacrificed his life in vain, father.

01:39:13.450 --> 01:39:17.350
It would be a blot on the Zabi family name if it were to be said that he died uselessly.

01:39:17.780 --> 01:39:20.040
It is our duty to vindicate his action.

01:39:20.800 --> 01:39:23.490
Karen, I don't know what you propose to do, but I...

01:39:23.490 --> 01:39:25.130
We got here as soon as we could, father.

01:39:25.890 --> 01:39:28.410
Welcome home, Dozel. And you, Kish.

01:39:30.120 --> 01:39:31.540
I wish there was something I could say.

01:39:31.680 --> 01:39:32.940
I give you my word, father.

01:39:33.140 --> 01:39:36.020
We'll track down that mobile suit and avenge our brother's death.

01:39:36.360 --> 01:39:36.900
It's unreal.

01:39:37.230 --> 01:39:38.570
I still cannot believe it happened.

01:39:38.790 --> 01:39:41.370
Somehow I expect him to walk in here full of life at any moment.

01:39:41.510 --> 01:39:43.090
We'll concentrate on winning the war.

01:39:43.350 --> 01:39:44.830
That's the best way to honor his memory.

01:39:45.060 --> 01:39:45.560
His way.

01:39:46.210 --> 01:39:51.960
I looked forward to the day Garma would finally receive promotion to a full admiralcy.

01:39:52.520 --> 01:39:54.320
What an honor to take orders from my brother.

01:39:54.670 --> 01:39:57.980
Son, it is not good to live in the past.

01:39:59.010 --> 01:39:59.970
Garma has left us.

01:40:00.350 --> 01:40:03.840
Accept it. Don't dwell on it. Put it behind you.

01:40:04.960 --> 01:40:07.920
The best way to honor Polgarma is to let him rest in peace.

01:40:28.110 --> 01:40:29.250
Has anyone seen Amuro?

01:40:29.430 --> 01:40:29.970
He said he was...

01:40:30.000 --> 01:40:34.600
going to visit his mother, actually. Ah, he must have been in that core fighter I saw leaving. I think

01:40:34.600 --> 01:40:39.900
he said that his home is about 30 kilometers east of here. Yeah, a native earth dweller? I knew that

01:40:39.900 --> 01:40:44.590
rat was one of the elite. Living on earth doesn't automatically make you one of the elite. Anyway,

01:40:44.830 --> 01:40:49.170
Amuro lived with his father on side seven. He told us he hardly ever gets to earth, and he hasn't

01:40:49.170 --> 01:40:54.230
seen his mother in ages. If you live on earth, you're one of the elite. There must have been an

01:40:54.230 --> 01:40:58.550
awful lot of heavy air raids around this area from the looks of all the bummed out buildings. Yeah,

01:40:58.550 --> 01:40:59.350
And that's not all.

01:41:00.410 --> 01:41:02.810
There's a lot of gorilla activity here. Very frightening.

01:41:30.060 --> 01:41:31.400
Glad to see you, haven't you?

01:41:31.400 --> 01:41:32.980
What are you drunks doing in my house?

01:41:33.140 --> 01:41:33.940
Who's drunk?

01:41:34.200 --> 01:41:34.620
Quiet.

01:41:34.940 --> 01:41:36.380
Sir, he insulted me.

01:41:36.780 --> 01:41:43.080
Sir, you found us in this condition, but this house has been abandoned.

01:41:43.520 --> 01:41:44.620
It's not abandoned.

01:41:45.200 --> 01:41:47.670
Look around. No one's here.

01:41:48.650 --> 01:41:50.130
Yeah, we'll see.

01:41:51.950 --> 01:41:52.510
Mother!

01:41:58.980 --> 01:41:59.840
Master's mommy!

01:42:01.000 --> 01:42:06.280
Most civilians evacuated when the air raids got so heavy.

01:42:06.640 --> 01:42:09.180
Yeah, the ones who were lucky enough to still be alive.

01:42:09.630 --> 01:42:11.650
All right, that's enough. Leave the kid alone.

01:42:12.110 --> 01:42:13.550
Somebody bring me another bottle.

01:42:13.900 --> 01:42:14.320
Yes!

01:42:23.600 --> 01:42:26.200
Amaro will be safer living with me on side seven.

01:42:26.400 --> 01:42:27.240
Please come with us.

01:42:27.440 --> 01:42:29.900
This is my home, and I won't be driven out of it.

01:42:30.000 --> 01:42:31.920
You know how to reach me if you change your mind,

01:42:31.940 --> 01:42:34.040
and I hope with all my heart that you will, dear.

01:42:34.200 --> 01:42:35.140
I'm sorry, darling.

01:42:35.360 --> 01:42:37.260
I'll just never be able to live in space.

01:42:37.500 --> 01:42:39.220
You'll be a good boy, Amuro, hear?

01:42:40.570 --> 01:42:41.950
My baby, goodbye.

01:42:42.500 --> 01:42:45.160
I hope when you're grown up, you might be able to understand.

01:42:59.380 --> 01:42:59.980
There's your money.

01:43:00.000 --> 01:43:01.120
Go pick it up.

01:43:04.410 --> 01:43:05.530
All right, thank you.

01:43:05.750 --> 01:43:06.030
What?

01:43:06.770 --> 01:43:07.630
You should be ashamed.

01:43:07.970 --> 01:43:09.450
Give that poor lady her money right now.

01:43:09.800 --> 01:43:11.140
Who do you think you are, huh?

01:43:12.400 --> 01:43:13.500
I've seen him before.

01:43:13.920 --> 01:43:15.620
You're headed for a lot of trouble, kid.

01:43:15.760 --> 01:43:16.620
I hope you know that.

01:43:16.990 --> 01:43:18.790
You disgrace the uniform you wear.

01:43:19.290 --> 01:43:20.950
Punk, I'm gonna get...

01:43:27.800 --> 01:43:29.820
You're gonna be swallowing your teeth, kid.

01:43:30.090 --> 01:43:33.090
I'll teach you a lesson you'll never forget until the day you die.

01:43:35.660 --> 01:43:36.880
Why, that's Amaro.

01:43:37.240 --> 01:43:38.020
Of course.

01:43:38.240 --> 01:43:40.580
My daughter's favorite childhood playmate.

01:43:41.000 --> 01:43:41.400
Oh, dear.

01:43:41.760 --> 01:43:42.620
Stop, please.

01:43:42.840 --> 01:43:43.720
He's just a boy.

01:43:43.980 --> 01:43:44.040
Stop.

01:43:44.920 --> 01:43:46.120
Mind your own business, woman.

01:43:46.240 --> 01:43:46.780
Take the fruit.

01:43:46.820 --> 01:43:47.960
You can have your money back.

01:43:48.140 --> 01:43:48.940
Just go away.

01:43:49.520 --> 01:43:49.960
Don't.

01:43:53.240 --> 01:43:55.020
The bomb attacks were terrifying.

01:43:55.590 --> 01:43:56.390
Every night.

01:43:56.700 --> 01:43:57.600
They never let off.

01:43:57.700 --> 01:43:57.920
I can't believe it.

01:43:58.370 --> 01:43:58.810
Calmly.

01:43:59.170 --> 01:43:59.970
How could she be dead?

01:44:00.510 --> 01:44:03.030
My daughter and my husband, the same night.

01:44:03.570 --> 01:44:05.870
Why was I chosen to be the only survivor?

01:44:07.920 --> 01:44:08.940
Have you seen your mother?

01:44:09.160 --> 01:44:10.120
She's in good health?

01:44:10.220 --> 01:44:10.860
She's gone.

01:44:11.200 --> 01:44:11.620
Oh, dear.

01:44:11.820 --> 01:44:13.320
You mean she didn't write to tell you?

01:44:13.460 --> 01:44:17.060
She's been working at the refugee camp as a volunteer for several months.

01:44:17.280 --> 01:44:17.760
Oh, really?

01:44:18.070 --> 01:44:19.370
Can you give me directions to it?

01:44:19.650 --> 01:44:20.070
Sure.

01:44:20.310 --> 01:44:22.890
It's on Church Hill where you and Comely used to play.

01:44:23.090 --> 01:44:23.750
Do you remember?

01:44:23.970 --> 01:44:26.230
You used to say it was uphill both ways.

01:44:26.310 --> 01:44:26.630
Thank you.

01:44:26.690 --> 01:44:26.870
Huh?

01:44:27.140 --> 01:44:27.460
What?

01:44:28.590 --> 01:44:29.970
Be careful and give your mother...

01:44:30.120 --> 01:44:31.060
my best regards.

01:44:32.580 --> 01:44:37.600
Port to battle station.

01:44:38.600 --> 01:44:41.150
Sir, they're 10 kilometers west over the ocean.

01:44:41.430 --> 01:44:43.890
There's no friendly IFF signal on any channel.

01:44:44.050 --> 01:44:46.090
Sir, shall I launch white base in combat mode?

01:44:46.130 --> 01:44:47.490
I don't want to give away our position

01:44:47.490 --> 01:44:48.730
if they don't know we're here.

01:44:48.770 --> 01:44:49.150
Then what?

01:44:49.250 --> 01:44:51.130
We'll just hope our fighters can bring them down

01:44:51.130 --> 01:44:53.690
in time for our rendezvous with the Madea transport plane.

01:44:53.870 --> 01:44:54.210
Yes, sir.

01:45:04.060 --> 01:45:13.860
Aircraft closing from behind too easy you're toast

01:45:33.870 --> 01:45:37.390
Now what? Looks to me like one of those Federal Forces warplanes.

01:45:37.430 --> 01:45:38.730
Now what would he be doing here?

01:45:38.790 --> 01:45:39.810
Bound to be more trouble.

01:45:40.720 --> 01:45:41.080
Hi.

01:45:41.510 --> 01:45:44.880
Oh, wow. Never seen a fighter up close on the ground.

01:45:46.120 --> 01:45:49.020
Wait just a minute, please. We'd like to speak to you.

01:45:49.020 --> 01:45:49.140
Huh?

01:45:50.810 --> 01:45:52.390
Obviously, with the Federal Forces.

01:45:52.710 --> 01:45:54.690
I don't know why you're here. You're not wanted.

01:45:54.870 --> 01:45:57.270
But may we at least ask you to hide that fighter plane?

01:45:57.590 --> 01:45:59.070
I don't understand. I just...

01:45:59.070 --> 01:45:59.670
Don't you know?

01:46:00.000 --> 01:46:03.060
The enemy's front-line base is there on top of that mountain behind you.

01:46:03.240 --> 01:46:05.820
You're putting us all in danger flying that military craft.

01:46:06.060 --> 01:46:09.020
They have artillery just waiting for a target like your fighter.

01:46:09.240 --> 01:46:10.580
Sorry. Thanks for warning me.

01:46:11.240 --> 01:46:11.420
Bro.

01:46:13.230 --> 01:46:13.450
Huh?

01:46:18.800 --> 01:46:20.530
Mother, you look great.

01:46:21.850 --> 01:46:23.650
You're real. I wasn't dreaming.

01:46:25.800 --> 01:46:26.780
No, you weren't.

01:46:26.840 --> 01:46:27.900
Amuro, darling.

01:46:28.980 --> 01:46:29.400
Mom!

01:46:30.510 --> 01:46:32.390
Oh, I missed you so much.

01:46:33.060 --> 01:46:34.760
I didn't know if you were dead or alive.

01:46:35.550 --> 01:46:37.330
Oh, I didn't know where you were.

01:46:43.320 --> 01:46:50.280
I don't want to seem insensitive,

01:46:50.460 --> 01:46:52.100
but we have to hide that fighter plane.

01:46:52.340 --> 01:46:53.020
I understand.

01:46:53.460 --> 01:46:54.380
Go ahead, son.

01:46:54.540 --> 01:46:55.980
We can talk when you get finished.

01:46:56.200 --> 01:46:58.080
I must have a million questions to ask you.

01:46:58.160 --> 01:46:59.560
Hurry, I've got it.

01:46:59.840 --> 01:46:59.940
Whatever.

01:47:00.060 --> 01:47:01.680
fine boy. Yes, he is.

01:47:11.730 --> 01:47:13.670
We're saying side seven was evacuated

01:47:13.670 --> 01:47:15.440
under enemy fire? That's right.

01:47:15.720 --> 01:47:18.170
And your father is among the missing?

01:47:18.450 --> 01:47:18.850
Yes.

01:47:20.510 --> 01:47:22.440
Inventors are searching the area!

01:47:22.820 --> 01:47:25.620
Okay, now don't make a move and don't speak a word.

01:47:25.900 --> 01:47:26.400
Understand?

01:47:38.920 --> 01:47:40.180
What kind of a fighter is that?

01:47:40.340 --> 01:47:40.900
You got me.

01:47:41.200 --> 01:47:42.780
Reconnaissance leader Hot Dog here.

01:47:43.170 --> 01:47:45.290
Enemy fighter of unknown design has been sighted.

01:47:45.590 --> 01:47:48.510
Northeast point 203, altitude 3,500 feet.

01:47:48.970 --> 01:47:49.330
Oh, no!

01:47:49.970 --> 01:47:50.490
Bye-bye.

01:48:00.124 --> 01:48:00.924
Big finish now.

01:48:01.404 --> 01:48:01.904
Let me go!

01:48:02.492 --> 01:48:03.332
Mm-hmm.

01:48:05.020 --> 01:48:05.380
Damn.

01:48:05.724 --> 01:48:08.724
I developed a leak in my fuel line.

01:48:11.868 --> 01:48:13.568
A lucky shot must have clipped my fuel line.

01:48:13.916 --> 01:48:15.556
They're badly damaged, but I can't pursue them.

01:48:15.776 --> 01:48:16.456
They're getting away.

01:48:16.656 --> 01:48:17.976
Can you estimate their bearing, Ryu?

01:48:18.176 --> 01:48:18.576
Southwest.

01:48:19.260 --> 01:48:20.160
I have to come in.

01:48:20.476 --> 01:48:23.356
Marker, are there any military installations located to the southwest?

01:48:23.356 --> 01:48:26.436
No, sir. Just a refugee camp a few miles from there. That's it.

01:48:26.436 --> 01:48:27.856
Armand Rowe went there to look for his mother.

01:48:28.508 --> 01:48:28.988
Say love.

01:48:29.148 --> 01:48:29.988
Cool armor room.

01:48:30.124 --> 01:48:30.424
Real.

01:48:30.828 --> 01:48:31.548
Do you need help?

01:48:31.884 --> 01:48:33.304
No, I can make it on my own.

01:48:33.548 --> 01:48:33.928
Thanks.

01:48:34.156 --> 01:48:35.416
Hurry back. Good work.

01:48:35.692 --> 01:48:36.492
Sorry that I lost them.

01:48:37.164 --> 01:48:38.464
It's vital we reach Amaro.

01:48:38.732 --> 01:48:39.292
Keep paging.

01:48:39.564 --> 01:48:40.224
I'll find him.

01:48:40.716 --> 01:48:43.496
Don't anybody make a move, just stay right where you are.

01:48:43.692 --> 01:48:44.852
We don't want to hurt anyone.

01:48:52.524 --> 01:48:53.724
We were sent here for your protection.

01:48:54.220 --> 01:48:57.620
We've had a report that an enemy fighter plane was seen landing in this area.

01:48:57.740 --> 01:48:59.980
If anyone has any information about it, report it.

01:49:00.000 --> 01:49:00.920
to me immediately.

01:49:01.200 --> 01:49:02.820
Whoever helps us find the pilot

01:49:02.820 --> 01:49:03.640
will be rewarded.

01:49:03.960 --> 01:49:04.780
How about that?

01:49:04.860 --> 01:49:05.740
He could win a medal

01:49:05.740 --> 01:49:06.680
and lots of candy.

01:49:06.900 --> 01:49:07.660
Leave us alone!

01:49:08.828 --> 01:49:10.328
Well, you see what I got here.

01:49:12.188 --> 01:49:13.408
A big bar of chocolate.

01:49:17.532 --> 01:49:17.972
well.

01:49:18.428 --> 01:49:20.868
If you don't want it, maybe some other boy will.

01:49:21.084 --> 01:49:21.684
We'll see.

01:49:26.364 --> 01:49:27.724
Well, somebody's being paged.

01:49:27.804 --> 01:49:28.164
Oh.

01:49:32.330 --> 01:49:33.910
All right, where's that beeper?

01:49:34.320 --> 01:49:37.140
That was just my hearing aid whistling.

01:49:37.240 --> 01:49:38.040
What's your problem?

01:49:38.500 --> 01:49:43.260
Hey, what is this?

01:49:43.460 --> 01:49:44.980
It's past noon and he...

01:49:45.000 --> 01:49:45.440
He's still asleep.

01:49:45.860 --> 01:49:46.220
Quiet.

01:49:46.480 --> 01:49:49.840
He's very ill and he needs all the sleep he can get, so don't awaken him.

01:49:49.960 --> 01:49:51.160
He mustn't be disturbed.

01:49:51.420 --> 01:49:52.520
I want to get a look at him.

01:50:34.412 --> 01:50:34.792
Uh-huh.

01:50:39.052 --> 01:50:41.512
Zeon will blame us for this. It's going to be real trouble.

01:50:41.752 --> 01:50:43.792
I know, but what can we do?

01:50:43.892 --> 01:50:44.532
I'm sorry.

01:50:50.476 --> 01:50:53.476
How? How could you deliberately take the life of a fellow man?

01:50:53.644 --> 01:50:54.144
Amaro!

01:50:54.572 --> 01:50:56.292
That man could have a wife and children.

01:50:57.356 --> 01:50:58.396
What's happened to you?

01:50:58.516 --> 01:50:59.076
What then?

01:50:59.340 --> 01:50:59.840
What?

01:51:00.188 --> 01:51:03.688
If you don't think I should kill our enemies, do you prefer that I let them kill me instead?

01:51:04.108 --> 01:51:05.908
Just what kind of a mother do I have here?

01:51:06.332 --> 01:51:07.772
Son, that was murder.

01:51:08.732 --> 01:51:11.572
Just declaring a war doesn't make killing people excusable.

01:51:11.852 --> 01:51:13.092
They murder us, don't they?

01:51:13.724 --> 01:51:14.944
Don't you care about me?

01:51:16.892 --> 01:51:17.532
Have you ever?

01:51:20.732 --> 01:51:22.272
You really did abandon me.

01:51:23.068 --> 01:51:24.068
What do you mean?

01:51:24.860 --> 01:51:27.640
My not going to side seven doesn't mean I abandoned you.

01:51:27.996 --> 01:51:29.096
You called me a murderer.

01:51:30.190 --> 01:51:30.910
Well, aren't you?

01:51:37.220 --> 01:51:38.360
Roger, go ahead.

01:51:39.950 --> 01:51:42.080
Emergent space is launching immediately.

01:51:42.440 --> 01:51:44.710
See that once to meet us at rendezvous point...

01:51:46.400 --> 01:51:47.260
I'm on my way now.

01:51:47.460 --> 01:51:49.650
Amaral, I love you.

01:51:49.690 --> 01:51:52.310
I only want you to be the sweet, gentle boy I remember.

01:51:52.710 --> 01:51:55.510
We didn't raise you to become a heartless monster, darling.

01:51:56.170 --> 01:51:58.800
We're at war. Everything's different.

01:52:02.720 --> 01:52:04.660
You make me ashamed to admit I'm your mother!

01:52:35.240 --> 01:52:39.420
Hey, a Zeke fighter. He's not going to make it very far.

01:52:39.850 --> 01:52:41.710
I'm not going to waste my time pursuing him.

01:52:41.960 --> 01:52:43.730
Why should I? I don't give a hoot.

01:52:43.890 --> 01:52:45.790
He might cause trouble for others, but not for me.

01:52:46.130 --> 01:52:53.080
Might as well check him out, but it's a white-based problem, not mine.

01:53:02.140 --> 01:53:08.640
I was afraid they weren't gonna make it get the emergency crew out there. Oh, no, this is a major base

01:53:08.640 --> 01:53:18.140
Daddy gotta do better than that

01:53:32.010 --> 01:53:36.820
Hey, the Medea! Of course! They're coming to fly cover for us! Great!

01:53:37.420 --> 01:53:49.450
What rotten luck. They didn't realize their rendezvous point was so near a major enemy base.

01:53:50.040 --> 01:53:50.360
Yeah!

01:54:02.010 --> 01:54:04.410
If I had raised him, he wouldn't have turned out this way.

01:54:04.800 --> 01:54:06.900
He was so gentle, he wouldn't have hurt a fly.

01:54:09.410 --> 01:54:11.210
What have they done to my poor Amaro?

01:54:26.150 --> 01:54:27.870
That ammunition we could have captured.

01:54:28.550 --> 01:54:29.970
Pearson, order all of our...

01:54:30.000 --> 01:54:31.140
to pull out of there now.

01:54:31.460 --> 01:54:31.820
Radio.

01:54:32.040 --> 01:54:32.280
Right.

01:54:32.620 --> 01:54:32.860
Right.

01:54:37.140 --> 01:54:38.400
Throwing precious supplies.

01:54:38.620 --> 01:54:39.640
Pull out of there immediately.

01:54:40.980 --> 01:54:41.580
Follow us.

01:54:41.700 --> 01:54:42.300
We'll cover.

01:54:43.810 --> 01:54:44.570
We're retreating?

01:54:47.950 --> 01:54:49.070
Is there somewhere we can take

01:54:49.070 --> 01:54:50.150
white base for repairs?

01:54:50.370 --> 01:54:50.930
And what do we do

01:54:50.930 --> 01:54:51.750
with all those civilians?

01:54:52.050 --> 01:54:53.210
I'll set up a new rendezvous

01:54:53.210 --> 01:54:53.990
at Point W,

01:54:54.170 --> 01:54:55.290
200 clicks north of here.

01:54:55.430 --> 01:54:56.290
And don't ask me

01:54:56.290 --> 01:54:56.910
what I want to do

01:54:56.910 --> 01:54:57.890
with the damn civilians.

01:55:10.780 --> 01:55:12.940
So does this mean you don't want to stay here with me?

01:55:13.410 --> 01:55:15.570
I wish I could, but I have a greater responsibility

01:55:15.570 --> 01:55:17.190
to all my friends aboard that ship.

01:55:24.740 --> 01:55:26.600
It's a real honor to meet Amaro's mother.

01:55:27.060 --> 01:55:29.640
I appreciate you having taken such good care of him.

01:55:30.030 --> 01:55:33.690
I don't exaggerate when I say we all owe our lives to your heroic son, madam.

01:55:34.080 --> 01:55:35.920
Did you say heroic, Amaral?

01:55:36.280 --> 01:55:38.140
He has served well above the call of duty,

01:55:38.140 --> 01:55:40.580
and you have every reason to be very proud of your son.

01:55:40.740 --> 01:55:42.340
How kind of you to say so.

01:55:42.690 --> 01:55:44.980
So, we have to launch right away.

01:55:45.860 --> 01:55:47.920
Have you decided what you're going to do, Amaral?

01:55:47.960 --> 01:55:53.300
Yes, I have. Goodbye.

01:55:54.130 --> 01:55:54.570
But I...

01:55:54.570 --> 01:55:55.450
Stay well, mother.

01:55:56.230 --> 01:55:56.990
Please write to me.

01:55:57.400 --> 01:55:58.120
I'll write back.

01:56:01.470 --> 01:56:03.790
Be assured, I'll watch after him like a brother.

01:56:30.480 --> 01:56:31.440
You

01:57:12.190 --> 01:57:12.890
Clear ahead, sir.

01:57:13.500 --> 01:57:15.020
Rendez-vous point W, sailor.

01:57:46.760 --> 01:57:48.620
We should have the engine repairs done by sunup.

01:57:49.490 --> 01:57:51.010
Well, I have a few minutes free now.

01:57:51.270 --> 01:57:52.630
You said you had some questions for me?

01:57:53.410 --> 01:57:57.010
For one thing, I'm wondering why you haven't given my crew any training discipline.

01:57:57.210 --> 01:57:59.970
According to every evaluation I've heard or read, the performance...

01:58:00.000 --> 01:58:03.600
The performance of the white base crew has exceeded all expectations we'd ever hoped for.

01:58:04.230 --> 01:58:07.370
The top brass have decided to keep the ship under your command.

01:58:07.840 --> 01:58:11.120
Your first assignment is in Europe, where we're launching a major new offensive.

01:58:11.420 --> 01:58:15.200
At the same time, we'll investigate all these rumors we keep hearing about new types.

01:58:15.500 --> 01:58:18.240
Uh, what are new types? I haven't heard the rumors.

01:58:18.460 --> 01:58:22.600
You will. They're like super espers.

01:58:22.740 --> 01:58:26.300
They have fantastic mental energies and powers of intuition so incredible

01:58:26.300 --> 01:58:28.660
that many people are tempted to believe they're supernatural.

01:58:28.660 --> 01:58:29.980
Mmm, if only

01:58:30.000 --> 01:58:33.940
If we had a few people like that working with us, we could get rid of the Zeons in no time at all.

01:58:34.630 --> 01:58:37.380
By the way, congratulations, Lieutenant JG.

01:58:37.520 --> 01:58:42.820
Huh? Is that a promotion? I'm a... what? What's the matter, Amuro?

01:58:43.280 --> 01:58:45.020
Huh? Matter? What do you mean?

01:58:45.300 --> 01:58:48.080
You ought to be sleeping. It's well past your bedtime, kid.

01:58:48.180 --> 01:58:48.960
Yeah, right.

01:58:49.340 --> 01:58:49.740
Amuro?

01:58:50.360 --> 01:58:50.620
Yes?

01:58:52.650 --> 01:58:57.280
Being a pilot is a big responsibility. Part of your job is getting a healthy amount of rest.

01:58:57.520 --> 01:58:58.640
I will. Thank you.

01:59:00.510 --> 01:59:02.610
Good night, ma'am. Good night, Lieutenant J.G.

01:59:08.520 --> 01:59:10.020
Came by to see you. Where were you?

01:59:10.180 --> 01:59:11.560
I stepped out to the lounge for a minute.

01:59:12.080 --> 01:59:13.700
The lounge is that way, Amuro.

01:59:16.950 --> 01:59:21.460
All right, so what? What's wrong with you?

01:59:21.840 --> 01:59:24.650
Nothing's wrong. Good night, Amuro. Sleep well.

01:59:24.910 --> 01:59:25.730
Let's go, Haro.

01:59:28.540 --> 01:59:29.400
What's with her?

02:00:03.000 --> 02:00:05.340
Well, good to see you. I hope you had breakfast.

02:00:08.280 --> 02:00:10.040
Amuro, have you had breakfast yet?

02:00:10.100 --> 02:00:11.660
No, sir. Not yet, sir.

02:00:12.530 --> 02:00:15.370
Do it now. We're going to be flying through Zeon territory.

02:00:15.840 --> 02:00:17.400
Gundam will be on combat alert.

02:00:17.720 --> 02:00:19.180
I will. Right away, sir.

02:00:30.350 --> 02:00:32.690
Matilda's escape route, sir, and here's Whiteface's route.

02:00:32.850 --> 02:00:35.750
We currently project a blanket all clear for both of these courses.

02:00:35.870 --> 02:00:37.930
We'll be safer flying over the ocean on our way to Europe.

02:00:38.130 --> 02:00:39.310
Oh, that's right. Launch!

02:00:39.630 --> 02:00:57.340
I don't want people to laugh at me or say I was made an admiral just because I'm your son.

02:00:57.940 --> 02:00:59.980
That's why I don't plan to return to Dion until...

02:01:00.090 --> 02:01:01.850
After I have achieved a triumphant victory,

02:01:03.170 --> 02:01:05.070
there will be no room for doubt in anyone's mind.

02:01:05.650 --> 02:01:07.210
And I want you to have real reason.

02:01:07.620 --> 02:01:08.320
Proud of me, Father.

02:01:09.960 --> 02:01:12.520
Forward to the opportunity of proving my worthiness.

02:01:20.790 --> 02:01:23.510
You mustn't let your grief cause you to neglect your duties.

02:01:25.200 --> 02:01:28.020
I hope you can forgive me for speaking so boldly, Highness.

02:01:28.490 --> 02:01:29.970
But it's important that you make an...

02:01:30.880 --> 02:01:32.780
Your people need to see their...

02:01:32.780 --> 02:01:33.620
Very well, Kish.

02:02:17.310 --> 02:02:19.090
Champ, what's everybody so excited about?

02:02:19.430 --> 02:02:23.070
We've located an unidentified ship of a type I've never seen before.

02:02:23.310 --> 02:02:24.250
Okay, bring it up.

02:02:27.200 --> 02:02:28.520
Is that the Trojan horse, sir?

02:02:29.430 --> 02:02:29.830
Romba.

02:02:30.000 --> 02:02:32.640
Could it be we'll have the opportunity of avenging Master Garma?

02:02:32.680 --> 02:02:34.280
Let's not be so hasty, Humlin.

02:02:35.910 --> 02:02:38.730
We've just begun re-entry, so we're helpless to do anything.

02:02:39.150 --> 02:02:42.030
And we're too far from the base to call fighters out here in time.

02:02:42.230 --> 02:02:44.230
After we clear re-entry, we can launch Zanzibar.

02:02:44.310 --> 02:02:46.750
But we have no fighter backup, just re-entry capsules.

02:02:48.350 --> 02:02:49.550
We need fighters.

02:02:50.740 --> 02:02:53.180
So exactly what are we going to do? Just let them get away?

02:02:54.290 --> 02:02:57.110
I have standing orders to avenge the son of Dejin.

02:02:57.480 --> 02:02:59.900
And when you receive a direct order from an admiral...

02:03:00.000 --> 02:03:01.320
It is not to be taken lightly.

02:03:01.600 --> 02:03:04.000
You'll have time to make plans while we're in re-entry.

02:03:04.180 --> 02:03:06.520
And I have every confidence you'll think of something, sir.

02:03:06.520 --> 02:03:08.940
I sincerely appreciate your vote of confidence, Haman.

02:03:09.100 --> 02:03:11.040
I only wish I felt similar assurance.

02:03:30.190 --> 02:03:31.610
Are you still doing repair work?

02:03:31.730 --> 02:03:31.950
Yeah.

02:03:33.380 --> 02:03:35.520
You don't look well, Amuro. What's wrong?

02:03:35.800 --> 02:03:36.640
Nothing's wrong, Haro.

02:03:37.400 --> 02:03:38.380
What are you working on?

02:03:38.660 --> 02:03:39.380
Computer unit.

02:03:40.060 --> 02:03:42.200
Don't forget to eat your dinner before it gets cold.

02:03:42.460 --> 02:03:43.040
Right, right.

02:03:45.660 --> 02:03:48.640
Amuro, your brainwave readings have fallen distressingly low.

02:03:48.860 --> 02:03:49.660
I'm all right.

02:03:51.070 --> 02:03:52.950
Come on, Haro. He doesn't want to be bothered.

02:03:56.950 --> 02:03:58.390
You'll return later to pick up the dishes.

02:03:58.550 --> 02:03:59.590
Don't wear yourself out.

02:04:01.500 --> 02:04:02.740
I think that just about does it.

02:04:04.080 --> 02:04:04.440
Yeah.

02:04:05.160 --> 02:04:06.780
Now then, I guess I better go eat dinner.

02:04:35.720 --> 02:04:37.820
Giran, I haven't seen Shaw. Where is he?

02:04:38.620 --> 02:04:42.250
I would imagine Shaw has rejoined his unit, wherever that is.

02:04:42.810 --> 02:04:43.410
I see.

02:04:51.780 --> 02:04:52.620
Yes, at once.

02:05:05.080 --> 02:05:06.720
Intensify portside firing!

02:05:06.940 --> 02:05:09.400
Pardon me, sir. Shall I take evasive maneuvers?

02:05:09.400 --> 02:05:11.500
We might be able to hide in those clouds to starboard.

02:05:11.900 --> 02:05:13.440
That storm looks like a bad one.

02:05:13.720 --> 02:05:18.240
It is a bad one.

02:05:20.260 --> 02:05:22.240
It's like the end of the world. What happened?

02:05:22.360 --> 02:05:24.360
Don't worry. The Gundam will protect us.

02:05:26.880 --> 02:05:28.580
I have to admit, it's pretty scary.

02:05:28.920 --> 02:05:29.980
Maybe the Zeons have a new...

02:05:30.920 --> 02:05:35.890
It looks like the Fettys are using a new secret weapon, sir.

02:05:36.700 --> 02:05:38.600
No, it's a natural phenomenon on Earth.

02:05:38.760 --> 02:05:39.680
They call it lightning.

02:05:41.040 --> 02:05:42.700
There's really no cause for alarm.

02:05:42.880 --> 02:05:44.600
I've seen this often on my trips to Earth.

02:05:45.500 --> 02:05:46.960
Don't fret about any danger.

02:05:47.180 --> 02:05:49.040
Just try to appreciate the beauty of it all.

02:05:49.380 --> 02:05:54.220
While we're hidden from sight, look for a place to bring us down.

02:05:54.320 --> 02:05:54.620
Yes, sir.

02:05:56.630 --> 02:05:59.070
Scan the surface immediately with infrared sensors.

02:05:59.310 --> 02:05:59.970
Check the terrain.

02:06:00.000 --> 02:06:07.910
with a laser scan as well marker confirm our heading and entry angle that's going to be a tight

02:06:07.910 --> 02:06:29.290
squeeze with no margin for error mirai think you can handle it yes sir we have now come to zero speed

02:06:30.060 --> 02:06:31.760
Good. Well done, Mirai. I'm impressed.

02:06:32.300 --> 02:06:33.840
Now then, attention all sections.

02:06:34.200 --> 02:06:36.060
Activate anti-aircraft batteries at once.

02:06:36.240 --> 02:06:37.600
Mobile suits prepare for launch.

02:06:37.880 --> 02:06:40.370
Amuro, are you still here lying around and moping?

02:06:40.640 --> 02:06:41.860
What am I gonna do with him?

02:06:42.020 --> 02:06:43.360
Hurry! We gotta go!

02:06:49.680 --> 02:06:50.840
Come on, snap out of it, Amuro.

02:06:51.060 --> 02:06:52.540
I'm not gonna let you give in this thing.

02:06:52.840 --> 02:06:53.660
Leave me alone.

02:06:53.820 --> 02:06:55.000
Listen, come off it.

02:06:55.040 --> 02:06:57.400
You're endangering yourself and a lot of others acting this way.

02:06:57.460 --> 02:06:58.640
Mind your own business, Rio.

02:06:58.660 --> 02:06:59.720
No more fooling around.

02:07:00.000 --> 02:07:01.040
Let go.

02:07:01.880 --> 02:07:03.950
You can be persuasive when you want.

02:07:06.840 --> 02:07:09.080
There they go. Let's hope they didn't spot us.

02:07:13.630 --> 02:07:14.770
Yeah, that was them, all right.

02:07:14.930 --> 02:07:16.930
Right, the magnetic signature topped off the scale.

02:07:17.070 --> 02:07:18.890
Notify FW with a signal flare.

02:07:21.660 --> 02:07:23.600
Horse sat down and is hiding on land, sir.

02:07:23.840 --> 02:07:25.860
We pinpointed their location with MagnoScan.

02:07:25.960 --> 02:07:28.040
Transmit the coordinates to our computer at once.

02:07:28.360 --> 02:07:28.680
Yes, sir.

02:07:28.960 --> 02:07:29.980
Stand by to set a new...

02:07:30.000 --> 02:07:38.180
course enemy clothing launch cover fire give us a missile umbrella and prepare a gun dam and gun

02:07:38.180 --> 02:07:49.820
cannon for a quick launch on my command blast we have the elusive trojan horse inside our scanner

02:07:49.820 --> 02:07:59.620
range start collecting data this is how i always want to remember you

02:08:00.220 --> 02:08:04.220
It's such a thrill to see you charging into battle personally instead of just giving orders.

02:08:05.220 --> 02:08:07.360
This is something I have to handle personally.

02:08:07.560 --> 02:08:08.840
There's too much riding on it.

02:08:11.020 --> 02:08:12.460
Nobody but my team goes in.

02:08:13.340 --> 02:08:14.040
Coase! Coase!

02:08:14.220 --> 02:08:15.180
Ready to launch, sir.

02:08:16.030 --> 02:08:16.650
Ready, sir!

02:08:23.330 --> 02:08:25.270
Concentrating our attention on the Trojan horse.

02:08:25.270 --> 02:08:27.990
They'll no doubt send their mobile suits out to lure us away.

02:08:28.270 --> 02:08:29.970
Don't let that kind of trickery take you in.

02:08:30.000 --> 02:08:30.780
Yes, sir.

02:08:30.960 --> 02:08:31.980
Are we cleared for launch?

02:08:32.220 --> 02:08:33.900
Launch bay doors are opening now.

02:08:34.080 --> 02:08:35.840
Their mobile suits are no match for us.

02:08:35.940 --> 02:08:37.100
Just knock them out of your way.

02:08:52.070 --> 02:08:54.790
We've held them down as long as we could, but we're hopelessly outgunned,

02:08:54.790 --> 02:08:56.130
and I need to get my men out of here.

02:08:56.330 --> 02:08:57.610
Request permission to withdraw.

02:08:58.140 --> 02:08:59.820
Well done. Return to base immediately.

02:09:00.020 --> 02:09:02.320
Lieutenant Ranba will be taking over from here.

02:09:02.500 --> 02:09:04.440
Attack wing, disengage, and return to base.

02:09:06.230 --> 02:09:07.650
Lieutenant Bright, look at that.

02:09:07.770 --> 02:09:08.890
Those commasai's pulled out.

02:09:08.990 --> 02:09:10.990
Now's our chance to execute our escape plan.

02:09:11.250 --> 02:09:11.670
Stand by.

02:09:13.290 --> 02:09:15.550
Ryu, are you and Amuro standing by for a launch?

02:09:15.590 --> 02:09:15.830
Negative.

02:09:16.420 --> 02:09:16.940
What do you mean?

02:09:17.140 --> 02:09:19.060
Amuro's emotionally exhausted, Lieutenant Bright.

02:09:19.240 --> 02:09:20.920
He's walking around like some kind of zombie.

02:09:21.080 --> 02:09:21.840
I won't have it.

02:09:22.130 --> 02:09:23.910
He can have his breakdown some other day.

02:09:24.070 --> 02:09:25.650
I want him ready to launch right now.

02:09:25.650 --> 02:09:27.530
I'll try and wake him up, but it won't be easy.

02:09:28.280 --> 02:09:28.920
Come on, Amuro.

02:09:29.450 --> 02:09:29.970
Time to go to work.

02:09:30.600 --> 02:09:32.920
I'll just have to leave it up to you, whether to launch or not.

02:09:33.200 --> 02:09:33.940
I have to get out there.

02:09:37.560 --> 02:09:40.740
Amuro, I sure hope you're ready, because we have you locked into the catapult.

02:09:41.100 --> 02:09:42.200
Please tell me that you're awake.

02:09:42.380 --> 02:09:44.220
You can go ahead and launch me, Sailor. I'm ready.

02:09:44.660 --> 02:09:46.280
You don't sound alert. What's wrong?

02:09:46.740 --> 02:09:48.690
I'm awake now. I'm on my way, Ryu.

02:09:49.040 --> 02:09:51.800
Maybe a bit of action will bring Amuro back to life, Sailor.

02:09:51.900 --> 02:09:54.280
Very well. Gundam is now clear for launching.

02:10:01.400 --> 02:10:03.340
What the? Huh?

02:10:18.760 --> 02:10:20.500
Cover fire. Blanket that hillside.

02:10:23.190 --> 02:10:24.610
All right. You've had it.

02:10:24.880 --> 02:10:26.240
You made the mistake of making me mad.

02:10:36.300 --> 02:10:38.010
Kuss, toss out a cracker.

02:10:38.260 --> 02:10:38.720
Huh?

02:10:55.080 --> 02:10:55.920
His rifle away.

02:10:56.550 --> 02:10:59.760
Oh no!

02:11:15.900 --> 02:11:18.330
And now it looks like they're launching a third one.

02:11:20.140 --> 02:11:21.040
Move on, Hayato.

02:11:21.360 --> 02:11:22.860
Amaro's going hand-to-hand with three of them.

02:11:23.120 --> 02:11:24.180
Give him cover fire, quick!

02:11:30.960 --> 02:11:34.920
So, you guys developed some new secret weapons, too. Gundam's ready for you.

02:11:35.320 --> 02:11:39.420
Watch out! We never know what to expect from these guys. Amro, be careful!

02:11:46.400 --> 02:11:52.550
Laser sword?

02:12:01.210 --> 02:12:03.710
Take the advantage when you've got it, or end up dead.

02:12:09.490 --> 02:12:10.130
Oh, man.

02:12:10.510 --> 02:12:13.850
That new Zaku has more power and heavier weapons than we ever suspected.

02:12:20.290 --> 02:12:21.670
Kuz, Kuzin, disengage.

02:12:21.830 --> 02:12:22.850
We're going back to the ship.

02:12:45.160 --> 02:12:46.600
All aboard and standing by.

02:12:46.870 --> 02:12:48.150
Blast out of here immediately.

02:12:48.450 --> 02:12:50.150
Full power, evasive maneuvering,

02:12:50.230 --> 02:12:51.970
and throw out the blinders to cover our retreat.

02:13:00.670 --> 02:13:01.550
I can't see anything.

02:13:32.400 --> 02:13:33.900
Hmm. Why did they run away?

02:13:35.180 --> 02:13:38.300
I don't know whether they gave up or if they just let us get away.

02:13:39.100 --> 02:13:43.320
This is both a tragic occasion and one of profound inspiration for all Zeons.

02:13:43.670 --> 02:13:46.910
I have lost a brother, and our people have lost a great hero.

02:13:47.230 --> 02:13:49.390
But we shall not surrender to our grief.

02:13:50.220 --> 02:13:54.720
We shall draw on his example and continue fighting on to avenge all our fallen loved ones.

02:13:54.880 --> 02:13:58.540
We will endure these sacrifices, and we will build our nation ever stronger.

02:13:59.000 --> 02:13:59.720
Don't give up.

02:14:02.220 --> 02:14:06.640
It's Gehran. They're broadcasting Garma's memorial ceremony on a worldwide network.

02:14:06.880 --> 02:14:08.680
He's using it for propaganda, of course.

02:14:09.640 --> 02:14:16.800
50 years a greedy clique of the elite have extended the Earth Federation's brutal control of space at our expense.

02:14:17.250 --> 02:14:22.330
We were forced to leave our beloved planet Earth in order to form space colonies for the Federation.

02:14:22.940 --> 02:14:28.840
And how many times since then has the Federation turned a deaf ear to our pleas for freedom, independence and equality?

02:14:28.840 --> 02:14:29.900
What we no longer

02:14:34.440 --> 02:14:37.580
He was eager to die.

02:14:44.900 --> 02:14:45.340
Bartender.

02:14:45.710 --> 02:14:48.250
Allow me the honor of buying you that drink, young man.

02:14:48.910 --> 02:14:50.410
Can I join you?

02:14:50.650 --> 02:14:51.970
Thank you very much.

02:14:52.470 --> 02:14:54.310
Well, sir, let me guess.

02:14:54.470 --> 02:14:56.050
You're with the Royal Guard, right?

02:14:57.420 --> 02:14:58.580
Is it that obvious?

02:14:59.170 --> 02:14:59.910
One of Kashiris.

02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:08.350
very good command you have a sharp eye are you sure you're all right now amaro i realize i

02:15:08.350 --> 02:15:14.620
